t can also make you feel dizzy when you spin around quickly! This is because of the fluid in the cochlea’s tubes, which moves as you spin. It keeps going for a while after you stop, giving you the impression that you are still moving.","etag":"ef5c-108620"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/The human ear can differentiate between up to <b>400,000 tones</b> and can even tell which direction they are coming from.","etag":"5d7f-43245"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/The individual tones, noises and speech we hear are made up of vibrating air particles known as sound waves. These sound waves are collected by the pinna and travel through the ear canal into the ear.","etag":"0ed3-69741"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/The parts of the ear that we can see are the pinna, the earlobe and the opening of the ear canal. However, most important parts of the ear are inside our head and are not visible from outside.","etag":"b1c9-66717"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/The sound waves pass through the ear canal to reach the auditory nerve, which is connected to the brain. The brain translates the signals sent to it so that we can hear.","etag":"0a0d-55917"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/a barking dog coming from behind","etag":"22b2-13581"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/a fire alarm ringing","etag":"0d87-9693"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/cars approaching on the motorway","etag":"765c-11277"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/ear canal","etag":"9bb9-6381"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/ear lobe","etag":"22dd-6093"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/pinna","etag":"4554-4365"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/Fill in the gaps.","etag":"7a75-11520"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/Label the visible parts of the ear.","etag":"ed11-16992"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/Our hearing can warn us of dangers in our environment. Match the danger to the picture.","etag":"9870-37296"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/What can you hear?","etag":"0919-11520"}],"svgs":[{"fileId":"svg/c-svg/2021/01/19-2017-10-23-ear.svg","etag":"d568-7380"}],"lsg